      "writtenOn": "2019-03-01T21:31:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can we delete the code associated with security.restorecon_last? This xattr was set at the top level directory, and represents the hash of all the file_contexts files. Presumably security.partial_match_digest at this upper level would consist of the majority of hashes which would have been in file_contexts anyway. So it seems like this is now redundant.",
      "revId": "6410782727f8c1a4b5fdcac1988c659019a80a91",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2cace40a_9a3024f9",
        "filename": "libselinux/src/android/android_platform.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 1663,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003966
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-01T21:31:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can we avoid the /data special case here? Presumably we want this to apply to all directories, not just /data directories. For example, this same optimization could apply to the /persist partition.",
      "revId": "6410782727f8c1a4b5fdcac1988c659019a80a91",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "86c9f74a_c53c30b8",
        "filename": "libselinux/src/android/android_platform.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 1670,
