    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e090c7b1_bdef728e",
        "filename": "libselinux/src/android/android_platform.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 1730,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003966
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-01T21:31:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why are you deferring setting the RESTORECON_PARTIAL_MATCH_DIGEST until the end, instead of doing it near line 1677? It seems like you could check setrestoreconlast at that point, no?\n\n(I guess it would depend on the order of the tree walk, since presumably you wouldn\u0027t want to mark the directory as completed until all the subelements of the directory tree have been completed. I don\u0027t recall what walk order is used here...)",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1721,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1730,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "6410782727f8c1a4b5fdcac1988c659019a80a91",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a876476f_c0509c73",
        "filename": "libselinux/src/android/android_platform.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 1730,
      "author": {
        "id": 1088085
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-01T21:50:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I thought about setting the digest after visiting the subdirs. Then I wonder if the error elsewhere could actually indicate a problem in file context. Anyway, if we want to set early, we could use the postorder directory FTS_DP, and maybe convert part of the loop into recursion.",
      "parentUuid": "e090c7b1_bdef728e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1721,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1730,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "6410782727f8c1a4b5fdcac1988c659019a80a91",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7198eed8_92fa0284",
        "filename": "libselinux/src/android/android_platform.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 1730,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003966
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-01T21:58:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The file_contexts files are validated at compile time. If we\u0027re seeing runtime misconfigurations in this file, it\u0027s probably better to abort() hard and make sure we have the appropriate compile time fixes in place.\n\nAs for directory tree walk order, I\u0027m fine either way. We could defer adding the hash to all the directories until the end, or add the hash as we finish the elements of the directory. I don\u0027t have a strong opinion either way. Whatever keeps the code simple.",
      "parentUuid": "a876476f_c0509c73",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1721,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1730,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "6410782727f8c1a4b5fdcac1988c659019a80a91",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
