      "writtenOn": "2019-03-01T21:31:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "variable length arrays are really error prone and dangerous to use. It would be safer and simpler to replace line 1049 with:\n\n  char *line;\n  asprintf(\u0026line, \"%s%s\", regex_str, ctx_raw);\n\nwhich will allocate an appropriate sized array for you.\n\nHaving said that, see comment on line 1050.",
      "revId": "6410782727f8c1a4b5fdcac1988c659019a80a91",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a8852c3e_b8f2d2f6",
        "filename": "libselinux/src/label_file.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 1050,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003966
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-01T21:31:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think it\u0027s necessary to concatenate the strings (line 1049), then call Sha1Update on the concatenated string. Just make two calls to Sha1Update:\n\n  Sha1Update(\u0026context, regex_str, strlen(regex_str));\n  Sha1Update(\u0026context, ctx_raw, strlen(ctx_raw));\n\nwhich has the same effect, but avoids additional memory allocations and string management code.",
      "revId": "6410782727f8c1a4b5fdcac1988c659019a80a91",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
